{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For there is not.</b> He returned to explain the matter of 'do not be overly righteous,' and its meaning is: know that you cannot avoid sinning, for there is no man who does not sin in deed or in speech or in thought, as written in the book of Proverbs among the seven abominations, 'one who devises thoughts of wickedness,' and the meaning of 'who does good always and never sins.'"], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:10.125131922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}